<http://data.silknow.org/object/16877e2e-fe96-3204-9045-df7b8e0945b0/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Woven silk and metal thread and cotton, plain weave ground and binding\nWarp: red silk\nWeft: red and blue silk\nMetal thread: silver strip open S-wound on yellow silk core.\nFive pieces sewn together.\nBlue ground with a lobed lattice worked in metal thread with red silk spots. The compartments contain one of two variations of the same arrangement: a star-like rosette in metal thread with a red silk centre surrounded by either a circle or a square, also in metal and red silk.  Radiating from this are stylised leaves and flowers.  At the upper edge of two pieces there is a band of blue weft, probably marking the end of a loom piece. \nOne selvedge: two white cotton cords."@en ;
